&lt;p&gt;SumUp&#39;s tax function is scaling to match a business that now spans more than 40 entities. This role is a senior partner to the Head of Tax across the Group&#39;s tax agenda. You&#39;ll lead the implementation and operationalisation of corporate income tax, transfer pricing, and indirect tax strategy, and you&#39;ll help shape the positions and policies behind it. You&#39;ll bring your own judgement to the most important topics, from how Pillar Two, CbCR, and ATAD III affect our structure to how we manage tax risk in audits, and you&#39;ll help the Head of Tax turn those views into a clear Group direction. This role reports to the Global Head of Tax and will have an impact on SumUp&#39;s IPO readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead delivery of SumUp&#39;s tax agenda across corporate income tax, transfer pricing, and indirect tax, within the Group tax strategy set by the Head of Tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the transfer pricing framework and its implementation, and propose improvements to both substance and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and maintain tax policies, controls, and governance documentation for Group entities, for sign-off by the Head of Tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the first point of contact for tax authority audits and controversies, keeping the Head of Tax aligned on positions and exposure&lt;/li&gt;
